{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"P10354","uniProtkbId":"CMGA_RAT","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"1989-07-01","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-09-02","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"1989-07-01","entryVersion":151,"sequenceVersion":1},"annotationScore":5.0,"organism":{"scientificName":"Rattus norvegicus","commonName":"Rat","taxonId":10116,"lineage":["Eukaryota","Metazoa","Chordata","Craniata","Vertebrata","Euteleostomi","Mammalia","Eutheria","Euarchontoglires","Glires","Rodentia","Myomorpha","Muroidea","Muridae","Murinae","Rattus"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"Chromogranin-A"},"shortNames":[{"value":"CgA"}]},"contains":[{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"Pancreastatin"}}},{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"Beta-granin"}}},{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"WE-14"}}},{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"Catestatin"}}},{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"GE-25"}}},{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"22459152"}],"value":"Serpinin-RRG"}}},{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"22459152"}],"value":"Serpinin"}}},{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"p-Glu serpinin precursor"}}}],"flag":"Precursor"},"genes":[{"geneName":{"value":"Chga"}}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"value":"Strongly inhibits glucose induced insulin release from the pancreas"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION","molecule":"Pancreastatin"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P10645"}],"value":"Catestatin inhibits catecholamine release from chromaffin cells and noradrenergic neurons by acting as a non-competitive nicotinic cholinergic antagonist. Can induce mast cell migration, degranulation and production of cytokines and chemokines"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P26339"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"22459152"}],"value":"Serpinin regulates granule biogenesis in endocrine cells by up-regulating the transcription of protease nexin 1 (SERPINE2) via a cAMP-PKA-SP1 pathway. This leads to inhibition of granule protein degradation in the Golgi complex which in turn promotes granule formation (By similarity). Serpinin and pGlu-serpinin can enhance both myocardial contractility (inotropy) and relaxation (lusitropy) and this cardio-stimulation requires a beta 1-adrenergic receptor/adenylate cyclase/cAMP/PKA pathway (PubMed:22459152)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P05059"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P10645"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"12388744"}],"value":"Self-interacts; self-assembly is promoted in vitro by chondroitin sulfate attachment which occurs at mildly acidic pH conditions (By similarity). Interacts with SCG3; this interaction is optimal in conditions mimicking the lumenal milieu of the trans-Golgi network, i.e. pH 5.5 and 10 mM Ca(+2) (PubMed:12388744). Interacts with ITPR1 in the secretory granules (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","note":{"texts":[{"value":"Associated with the secretory granule membrane through direct interaction to SCG3 that in turn binds to cholesterol-enriched lipid rafts in intragranular conditions. In pituitary gonadotropes, located in large secretory granules"}]},"subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"12388744"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"3896848"}],"value":"Cytoplasmic vesicle, secretory vesicle","id":"SL-0244"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"29166604"}],"value":"Cytoplasmic vesicle, secretory vesicle, neuronal dense core vesicle",